
# Benchmark prompt fixtures are compared by md5, and a comparison across hosts
# is only valid when the bytes are identical. A Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true rewrites LF to CRLF, which changes the digest: the
# fixtures pinned in AGENTS.md hash to 253c7ac5... and 37c5aad9... on Linux but
# to 46c8d967... and 06eb2ebe... after a CRLF checkout. Pin them to LF so every
# host reproduces the pinned md5.
#
# The two fixtures measured no throughput difference between CRLF and LF on
# gfx1100 (29.1 vs 29.0 and 27.2 vs 27.2 tok/s), so this is about reproducible
# fixture identity, not about a token-shape effect.
benchmarks/prompts/** text eol=lf
